  "summary": "Proposed v0.1.2-proposed.2 reconciles the complete supplied CLI transcript with current main. It defines interspersed option/value groups, literal boundaries, contextual help, ordinary-word aliases, stable scope and no product effects before complete validation. Retires the unreleased tgt ls proposal without reusing its spelling. Adds global syntax metadata and explicit named-option arity/repeatability; metadata checks reject collisions, inconsistent arity and command-prefix ownership changes. Updates docs, TODO, generated reference and existing native work gates. All 34 commands remain planned and their unresolved parameter contracts remain explicit. Actual suite: 154 tests ran, 152 passed and two skipped. Structural result: 858 checks, 71 concepts, 147 requirements, 36 work units, 29 schemas. All 36 planned AIDE exports pass passive pinned-schema validation. The 80 argv cases in 38 groups are unrun native expectations, not passed parser tests. This handoff precedes the authorized commit/push and does not grant acceptance or native implementation.",
